---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getPhotos } from "../utils/photos";

const timeline = [
  {
    date: "2020-2021",
    title: "Consultant I, InfoWorks",
  },
  {
    date: "2022-2024",
    title: "Consultant II, InfoWorks",
  },
  {
    date: "2024-Present",
    title: "Senior Consultant, InfoWorks",
  },
];

const photos = await getPhotos();
const featuredPhoto = photos.find((photo) => photo.slug === "dscf8520") ?? photos[0];
const featuredPhoto2 = photos.find((photo) => photo.slug === "dscf9704") ?? photos[0];
const featuredPhoto3 = photos.find((photo) => photo.slug === "dscf9241") ?? photos[0];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Sam Young"
  description="Learn more about Sam Young, a Nashville-based full-stack software engineer and designer."
>
  <div class="wrapper region prose flow">
    <h1>About me</h1>

    <p>
      I'm a full stack software engineer with a background in design, based out of
      Nashville, TN. I like translating what a project needs into something that's
      technically feasible, developer-friendly, and grounded in strong UX.
    </p>

    <section class="flow">
      <h2>Where I've been</h2>
      <ol class="timeline not-prose" role="list">
        {
          timeline.map((item) => (
            <li class="timeline__item">
              <div class="timeline__marker" aria-hidden="true" />
              <div class="timeline__content">
                <p class="timeline__date">{item.date}</p>
                <p class="timeline__title">{item.title}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>

    <div class="flow">
      <p>
        Most of that work leans on React, Angular, ASP.NET Core, and SQL
        Server, with Figma in the mix for client-facing prototyping. I have worked on
        projects ranging from a healthcare compliance platform, to an ROI
        calculator, to a document management system with bulk Excel workflows for a global
        financial client. You can see the fuller breakdown on my <a href="/resume">resume</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      Outside of client work, I like building things just to understand how
      they fit together. My <a href="/projects">projects</a> page has a
      storefront I built to learn headless commerce: Astro for the front
      end, Sanity for content, and Snipcart for cart and checkout. It's
      modeled on a real ultralight backpacking brand, so I could focus on
      the stack instead of inventing a catalog from scratch.
    </p>

    <div class="switcher">
      {featuredPhoto && (
        <a
          href={`/photography/${featuredPhoto.slug}/`}
          class=""
          aria-label="View this photo in the gallery"
        >
          <Image
            src={featuredPhoto.image}
            widths={[650, 800, 1400, 2000]}
            sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 75vw, calc(100vw - 2.75rem)"
            format="avif"
            quality={80}
            alt="View of a snowy mountain through the trees."
            loading="lazy"
            class="about-photo"
          />
        </a>
      )}
      {featuredPhoto2 && (
        <a
          href={`/photography/${featuredPhoto2.slug}/`}
          class=""
          aria-label="View this photo in the gallery"
        >
          <Image
            src={featuredPhoto2.image}
            widths={[650, 800, 1400, 2000]}
            sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 75vw, calc(100vw - 2.75rem)"
            format="avif"
            quality={80}
            alt="View of a snowy mountain through the trees."
            loading="lazy"
            class="about-photo"
          />
        </a>
      )}
      {featuredPhoto3 && (
        <a
          href={`/photography/${featuredPhoto3.slug}/`}
          class=""
          aria-label="View this photo in the gallery"
        >
          <Image
            src={featuredPhoto3.image}
            widths={[650, 800, 1400, 2000]}
            sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 75vw, calc(100vw - 2.75rem)"
            format="avif"
            quality={80}
            alt="View of a snowy mountain through the trees."
            loading="lazy"
            class="about-photo"
          />
        </a>
      )}
    </div>
    <p>
      When I'm not writing code, I am often outside with a camera. I keep a
      running <a href="/photography">photography</a> gallery here.
    </p>

    <p>
      I'm reachable through <a href="mailto:sam.young@email.com">email</a>, or
      you can view or download my <a href="/resume">resume</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
